<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<% locals.canonicalPath = '/privacy-policy'; %>
<% locals.breadcrumbs = [{ name:'Home', path:'/' }, { name:'Privacy Policy', path:'/privacy-policy' }]; %>
<%- include('partials/page-head') %>
</head>
<body class="lp-wrap">
<%- include('partials/navbar') %>

<section class="page-hero" style="padding-bottom:24px;">
  <div class="page-hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="lp-c" style="position:relative;z-index:1;">
    <%- include('partials/breadcrumb') %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-section" style="padding-top:0;">
  <div class="lp-c">
    <div class="legal-wrap">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last Updated: <%= lastUpdated %></p>

      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains what information StackifyX ("we", "us",
        "our") collects through the StackifyX website and platform (the
        "Service"), how we use it, and the choices you have. It describes our
        actual, current data practices — it does not describe features that
        are not yet part of the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>We collect information in the following categories, described in detail below:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Account information you provide when registering or signing in</li>
        <li>Project and inquiry information you submit</li>
        <li>Communication information exchanged through the platform</li>
        <li>Files you upload in connection with a project or inquiry</li>
        <li>Limited technical information collected automatically by our hosting infrastructure</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Account Information</h2>
      <p>When you create an account, we collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name, email address, and, optionally, phone number</li>
        <li>A securely hashed version of your password (we never store passwords in plain text)</li>
        <li>If you sign in with Google, your Google account ID, name, email and profile picture URL as provided by Google</li>
        <li>Account role (e.g. client or admin), account creation date, and last login date</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Project / Inquiry Information</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit a project inquiry or contact form, we collect the
        details you provide, which may include your name, email, phone,
        company name, project type, budget range, and a description of your
        project.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Communication Information</h2>
      <p>
        If you communicate with our team through the platform's messaging
        feature, we store those messages so both you and our team can refer
        back to the conversation as part of managing your project.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Uploaded Files</h2>
      <p>
        If you upload files in connection with a project or inquiry (such as
        reference documents or briefs), those files are stored so our team
        can access them while working on your project.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Automatically Collected Information</h2>
      <p>
        Like most web applications, our hosting infrastructure may log
        standard technical information (such as IP address, browser type,
        and request timestamps) for security and operational purposes. We do
        not currently use dedicated analytics or advertising tracking tools
        on the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Cookies and Sessions</h2>
      <p>
        We use a session cookie to keep you signed in after you log in. This
        cookie is required for authenticated features of the Service (such
        as your dashboard) to work, and is managed through our session
        store. We also use a small amount of browser local storage to
        remember your light/dark theme preference — this stays on your
        device and is not sent to our servers. We do not currently use
        third-party advertising or analytics cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>9. How We Use Information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To create and manage your account, including email verification and password resets</li>
        <li>To evaluate and respond to project inquiries and contact form submissions</li>
        <li>To communicate with you about your project</li>
        <li>To operate features such as the client and admin dashboards</li>
        <li>To process payments for active projects, where applicable</li>
        <li>To maintain the security and integrity of the Service</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>10. How We Share Information</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. We may share information
        with:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Service providers who help us operate the platform (such as our hosting provider, email delivery provider, and payment processor)</li>
        <li>Authorities, where required to comply with applicable law</li>
        <li>A successor entity, in the event of a business transfer, subject to the same protections described here</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>11. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        The Service integrates with third-party providers, including Google
        (for optional Google Sign-In), an email delivery provider (for
        account verification, notifications and password resets), and a
        payment processor (for handling payments on active projects). These
        providers process certain information as part of enabling that
        functionality and are subject to their own privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Data Storage and Security</h2>
      <p>
        Your information is stored in a MongoDB database. Passwords are
        hashed before storage and are never stored or displayed in plain
        text. We take reasonable measures appropriate to a platform of this
        size to protect your information, but no method of transmission or
        storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute
        security.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain account and project information for as long as your
        account is active or as needed to provide the Service to you. If you
        request account deletion, we will remove or anonymize your personal
        information except where we are required to retain it for legal,
        accounting, or legitimate business purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>14. User Rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may request to access, correct, or delete the personal
        information associated with your account by contacting us at
        <a href="mailto:stackifyx@gmail.com">stackifyx@gmail.com</a>. Depending
        on your location, you may have additional rights under applicable
        data protection law; we will respond to verified requests in
        accordance with applicable requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Account Deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Account deletion is currently handled manually. To request deletion
        of your account and associated personal information, please contact
        us at <a href="mailto:stackifyx@gmail.com">stackifyx@gmail.com</a>
        from the email address associated with your account.
      </p>

      <h2>16. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is intended for business and professional use and is not
        directed at children. We do not knowingly collect personal
        information from children. If you believe a child has provided us
        with personal information, please contact us so we can address it.
      </p>

      <h2>17. International Data Transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Our hosting and third-party service providers may process and store
        information in countries other than your own. Where this occurs, we
        rely on those providers' own safeguards for cross-border data
        handling.
      </p>

      <h2>18. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect
        changes to the Service or for legal or operational reasons. When we
        do, we will update the "Last Updated" date above. We encourage you to
        review this page periodically.
      </p>

      <h2>19. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how your
        information is handled, please contact us at
        <a href="mailto:stackifyx@gmail.com">stackifyx@gmail.com</a> or
        through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/site-footer') %>
</body>
</html>
